<section class="faq-page" style="padding: 60px 0 100px; background: #12110c;">
  <div class="page-width">
    
    <!-- Breadcrumb -->
    <nav style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-bottom: 24px;">
      <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}" style="color: inherit; text-decoration: none;">HOME</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span style="color: var(--color-primary); font-weight: 700;">FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS</span>
    </nav>

    <!-- Header -->
    <div style="text-align: center; max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto 48px;">
      <span style="font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; color: var(--color-primary); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.25em; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 12px; padding: 4px 12px; background: rgba(255, 217, 0, 0.1); border-radius: var(--radius-full);">
        TECHNICAL SUPPORT & FITMENT ANSWERS
      </span>
      <h1 style="font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 56px); font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.1; margin-bottom: 16px;">
        AUTOMOTIVE <span style="color: var(--color-primary);">LIGHTING FAQS</span>
      </h1>
      <p style="font-size: 16px; color: var(--color-text-muted); line-height: 1.6;">
        Everything you need to know about Canbus error decoding, bulb sizing, beam adjustment, legal compliance, and warranty coverage.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- FAQ Accordion List -->
    <div style="max-width: 840px; margin: 0 auto 64px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;">
      
      <div class="accordion-item open">
        <div class="accordion-header">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined" style="font-size: 22px; color: var(--color-primary);">memory</span>
            <span>Will Electro NightEye LED bulbs trigger Canbus dashboard error warnings?</span>
          </div>
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined" style="font-size: 20px; color: var(--color-text-muted);">expand_more</span>
        </div>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          No. Electro NightEye LED kits incorporate intelligent internal micro-decoders and EMC filters. They replicate factory halogen resistance and electromagnetic frequency, preventing dashboard bulb-out warning lights, radio static, and hyper-flashing on 99.9% of modern vehicles.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="accordion-item">
        <div class="accordion-header">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined" style="font-size: 22px; color: var(--color-primary);">build</span>
            <span>How difficult is the installation process? Do I need a mechanic?</span>
          </div>
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined" style="font-size: 20px; color: var(--color-text-muted);">expand_more</span>
        </div>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          Installation is 100% DIY plug-and-play. No wire cutting, splicing, or external ballast mounting is required. The bulb dimensions and socket collars match factory halogen units 1:1. Over 90% of motorists complete installation in their garage in under 10 minutes per side using standard hand tools.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="accordion-item">
        <div class="accordion-header">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined" style="font-size: 22px; color: var(--color-primary);">water_drop</span>
            <span>Can these bulbs withstand high-pressure car washes and deep puddles?</span>
          </div>
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined" style="font-size: 20px; color: var(--color-text-muted);">expand_more</span>
        </div>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          Yes. Electro NightEye bulbs are IP68 certified waterproof and submersible. The aircraft-grade 6063 aluminum housing is sealed with industrial triple-lip silicone O-rings, and the 12,000 RPM hydraulic turbo fan operates flawlessly even when completely submerged under water.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="accordion-item">
        <div class="accordion-header">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined" style="font-size: 22px; color: var(--color-primary);">wb_sunny</span>
            <span>Will these bulbs blind oncoming motorists?</span>
          </div>
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined" style="font-size: 20px; color: var(--color-text-muted);">expand_more</span>
        </div>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          No. Unlike cheap generic LED bulbs that scatter blinding light everywhere, Electro NightEye LEDs feature an ultra-thin 1.2mm copper board that places the CSP chips at the exact optical focal point of your headlight reflectors. This generates a razor-sharp horizontal cutoff line that illuminates the road ahead without blinding oncoming traffic.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="accordion-item">
        <div class="accordion-header">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined" style="font-size: 22px; color: var(--color-primary);">palette</span>
            <span>Which color temperature is best: 6500K Diamond White or 3000K Golden Amber?</span>
          </div>
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined" style="font-size: 20px; color: var(--color-text-muted);">expand_more</span>
        </div>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          <strong>6500K Diamond White</strong> provides optimal visual clarity, high contrast, and daylight illumination on dry highway tarmac. <strong>3000K Golden Amber</strong> is specifically engineered for severe weather—its longer wavelength cuts through dense fog, torrential monsoons, and snow without reflecting light back into the driver's eyes.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="accordion-item">
        <div class="accordion-header">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined" style="font-size: 22px; color: var(--color-primary);">shield</span>
            <span>What does the 2-Year Direct Replacement Warranty cover?</span>
          </div>
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined" style="font-size: 20px; color: var(--color-text-muted);">expand_more</span>
        </div>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          Our warranty covers all manufacturing defects, chip burnout, cooling fan failure, driver malfunction, and water intrusion for 24 full months. Simply contact our support team with a photo/video and your order number for an immediate replacement pair.
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- Contact Support Strip -->
    <div style="text-align: center; padding: 40px; background: rgba(255,217,0,0.04); border: 1px dashed var(--color-primary); border-radius: var(--radius-md); max-width: 840px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 8px;">STILL HAVE A QUESTION ABOUT YOUR CAR?</h3>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
        Our lighting specialists are available 24/7 to provide vehicle-specific advice and wiring verification.
      </p>
      <a href="/pages/contact" class="btn-primary" style="padding: 12px 28px; font-size: 13px;">
        CONTACT TECH SUPPORT
      </a>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "FAQ Page",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
